If your school has turned on **Show the library in the parent portal**, you can:

- **Search the catalogue** and see whether a book is on the shelf. You can never see who has it.
- See your child's **loans** (with due dates), **holds** and **fines**. Only titles the school shows
  to everyone appear.
- **Reserve** a book for your child, and cancel a reservation, if the school allows it.
- **Pay library fines online**, if the school takes online payments and allows it.

When a reserved book is ready, collect it from the library within the number of school days your
school sets. A weekly reminder is sent if your child has an overdue book and the school has turned
reminders on.

Library fines apply to students only.
